// `std.build`: the theories a project's manifest comes from. A package's
// `package.gandr` declares `module Package : Model(Gandr.Package)`, and a
// workspace's `workspace.gandr` declares a `Model(Gandr.Workspace)`.
// `gandr check` writes the manifest of each from its model. It writes
// `package.gandr.toml` or `workspace.gandr.toml` beside the source.
//
// No theory here states a law. An operation of each is a field the manifest
// records, and no conversion relates two of them. An operation carrying
// `@[ inert ]` is a field that only the manifest step and another inert
// declaration read. A package's address leaves such a field out.
// A package's name,
// version, authors, licence and addresses name the package without saying
// what it is.
//
// What a package depends on is not inert, and no model states it. A source
// imports a dependency by its coordinate, `import "path:../hello" as hello;`.
// `gandr check` commits each coordinate's address to the store and locks the
// pointer to it in the lock of the package. The package's address digests
// those addresses.
//
// Nor is what a package asks of the toolchain inert. `gandr check` refuses a
// package whose `Toolchain` the running toolchain does not meet. The
// package's address digests the constraint.
//
// A theory's presentation is a `Theory` value, and `modelType` computes the
// type of its models' entries from it: one value for each constant, in the
// order of the presentation, as nested pairs. `encode` folds a presentation
// and its entries together into one line for each constant. For
// `Gandr.Package`, the inert `packageEntries` reads a model's entries, and
// the inert `render` writes a model's lines. The equivalence of a package's
// model and its entries is checked in `corpus/model/desc/module-reflection.gandr`
// and not here: every package source imports this module, and the proof of
// the equivalence would cost each check of a package.
//
// Limits: an entry's sort is `String`, `Bool` or opaque. An opaque entry is
// the unit type, and the encoder writes no line for it, so a model with a
// constant of another sort has no equivalence to its entries. The encoder
// escapes no character of a string, because `std.string` has no operation on
// a character. One table holds every line, in the presentation's order, and
// the manifest step's tables wait on #4725. The checker unfolds `modelType`
// for at most 20 `String` constants or 14 `Bool` constants, and a wider
// presentation's type is undecided (#6181).
//
// - see: #533
// - see: #3029
// - see: #3030 — `Gandr`
// - see: #3072
// - see: #4527
// - see: #2993 — `Toolchain`
// - see: #6046 — `modelType`, `encode` and `render`
// - see: #6181 — the widest presentation `modelType` unfolds

/// The version a package and a workspace release at. [`Project`] brings it to
/// both, so a member reads its version from its workspace's model.
pub theory Versioned where {
  /// The version, as a package's manifest records it.
  @[ inert ]
  oper version : String;
}

/// What a package and a workspace ask of the toolchain that checks them.
/// [`Project`] brings it to both, so a member may read its constraints from
/// its workspace's model. A constraint is content, so the package's address
/// digests it. Each list is one line of `,`-separated entries, none when it
/// is empty, until an operation's port can be a list.
pub theory Toolchain where
  /// The least language version the sources target, `>= 0.3`, or empty for
  /// any.
  oper gandr : String;
  /// The features the sources use, each a feature's key in gandr's features
  /// ledger, which the toolchain implements whole or in part.
  oper features : String;
  /// The systems the package builds on, each `<architecture>-<os>` as
  /// `x86_64-linux`, or empty for any.
  oper systems : String;

/// What a package and a workspace both state: the version they release at
/// and what they ask of the toolchain. `Gandr.Package` and `Gandr.Workspace`
/// include it, so each takes the two theories it joins once.
pub theory Project where
  include Versioned;
  include Toolchain;

/// How a package's sources look: the `[presentation]` table of its
/// `package.gandr.toml`. The user's configuration file writes the same
/// table, and a
/// language server reads the package's table over the user's. Each field is
/// inert: how a source looks is not what it is.
pub theory Presentation where {
  /// The spelling a construct with a glyph takes, `unicode` or `ascii`, or
  /// empty to leave the reader's own.
  @[ inert ]
  oper spelling : String;
}

/// A package: the project a `package.gandr` roots. The model its
/// `module Package : Model(Gandr.Package)` declares describes it, and the
/// checker writes the project's `package.gandr.toml` from that model. Its own
/// fields are inert: its name, its authors, its documentation
/// and its presentation
/// leave its address alone. What it asks of the toolchain does not.
pub theory Gandr.Package where {
  include Project;
  include Presentation;
  /// The package's name, which the manifest records it by.
  @[ inert ]
  oper name : String;
  /// Who wrote the package, as one line, `Name <address>, Name <address>`: a
  /// list once an operation's port can be one.
  @[ inert ]
  oper authors : String;
  /// The package's licence, an SPDX expression.
  @[ inert ]
  oper licence : String;
  /// Where a reader finds the package's documentation.
  @[ inert ]
  oper documentation : String;
  /// The address a resolver may try first to fetch the package.
  @[ inert ]
  oper endpoint : String;
  /// The directory the package's modules sit under, a `/`-separated path
  /// from the package's root, `src`. The source `greet.gandr` in its `text`
  /// directory is the module `text.greet`. Discovery reads it as the string
  /// the model writes, before any source is checked, so the model states it as
  /// a string literal.
  @[ inert ]
  oper sources : String;
}

/// A workspace: the packages a `workspace.gandr` gathers, described by the
/// model its `module Workspace : Model(Gandr.Workspace)` is, beside the
/// `members` it names. The checker writes the `workspace.gandr.toml` of the
/// workspace from this model. Its members' package sources import it and read
/// what it states.
pub theory Gandr.Workspace where
  include Project;

/// A module of a package: a source below its package source. Its path from the
/// package's root names it, with `.` between segments, as `text.greet`. The
/// manifest lists each in `modules`. No source declares a model of it yet.
pub theory Gandr.Module where
  /// The module's path, with `.` between its segments.
  oper path : String;

/// The sort of a model's entry: a code for each type the encoder writes, and
/// one for any other sort.
pub data EntrySort : Type where
  /// `String`.
  | Text : EntrySort
  /// `Bool`.
  | Truth : EntrySort
  /// Any other sort. Its entry is the unit type, and the encoder writes no
  /// line for it.
  | Opaque : EntrySort

/// The code of the sort named `sort`. The comparison of two names computes
/// while a type is checked.
pub def entrySort(sort : String) -> EntrySort =
  if sort == "String" { Text } else if sort == "Bool" { Truth } else { Opaque }

/// The type of an entry whose code is `s`.
pub def entryType(s : EntrySort) -> -F Type =
  match s where
    | Text => return String
    | Truth => return Bool
    | Opaque => return Unit

/// The code of a constant's entry: the sort of its first output port, or
/// `Opaque` for a constant with none.
pub def portSort(outputs : Theory) -> EntrySort =
  match outputs where
    | Theory.Port(name, sort, indices, rest) => entrySort sort
    | _ => Opaque

/// An entry, then the entries after it.
pub data Entries(a : Type, b : Type) : Type where
  /// The entry `value`, then the entries `rest`.
  | Entry : (value : a, rest : b) --> Entries a b

/// The end of a model's entries.
pub data NoEntries : Type where
  /// No entry after this.
  | Ended : NoEntries

/// The type of the entries of a member chain: one entry for each constant.
/// A member that is no constant adds no entry.
def rec chainType(chain : Theory) -> -F Type =
  match chain where
    | Theory.Const(name, inputs, outputs, rest) => return (Entries (entryType (portSort outputs)) (chainType[<] rest))
    | Theory.Oper(name, inputs, outputs, rest) => chainType[<] rest
    | _ => return NoEntries

/// The type of the entries of a model of the presentation `presented`: one
/// entry for each constant, in the order of the presentation.
pub def modelType(presented : Theory) -> -F Type =
  match presented where
    | Theory.Presents(sorts, opers, rules) => chainType opers
    | _ => return NoEntries

/// The line of the constant `name` whose entry is `x`: `name = value` for a
/// string or a boolean, and no line for an opaque entry. A string is a TOML
/// basic string, its characters written as they are.
def line(name : String, s : EntrySort, x : entryType(s)) -> String =
  match s where
    | Text => string.append (string.append name " = \"") (string.append x "\"\n")
    | Truth => if x { string.append name " = true\n" } else { string.append name " = false\n" }
    | Opaque => ""

/// The lines of a member chain's entries `v`, one for each constant.
def rec chainLines(chain : Theory, v : chainType(chain)) -> String =
  match chain where
    | Theory.Const(name, inputs, outputs, rest) => match v where
      | Entry(x, r) => string.append (line name (portSort outputs) x) (chainLines[<] rest r)
    | Theory.Oper(name, inputs, outputs, rest) => chainLines[<] rest v
    | _ => ""

/// The lines of the entries `v` of a model of `presented`, one for each
/// constant, in the order of the presentation.
pub def encode(presented : Theory, v : modelType(presented)) -> String =
  match presented where
    | Theory.Presents(sorts, opers, rules) => chainLines opers v
    | _ => ""

/// The presentation of [`Gandr.Package`], from which its entries' type is
/// computed.
pub def packagePresentation : Theory = Gandr.Package;

/// The entries of the package model `m`, in the order of the presentation.
@[ inert ]
pub def packageEntries(m : Model(Gandr.Package)) -> modelType(packagePresentation) =
  Entry m.version (Entry m.gandr (Entry m.features (Entry m.systems (Entry m.spelling (Entry m.name (Entry m.authors (Entry m.licence (Entry m.documentation (Entry m.endpoint (Entry m.sources Ended))))))))))

/// The lines of the package model `m`, one for each constant, in the order
/// of the presentation: one table, with no escape.
@[ inert ]
pub def render(m : Model(Gandr.Package)) -> String =
  encode packagePresentation (packageEntries m)
